\p{The declines outside the R2 and mdata rows are older ones (metadata inside an inductive record, twice; a String literal without its prerequisites). Before this work the published engine gave 4 opposite verdicts on the R2 set as it stood then and 2 on S3's; in strict mode there is none now.}}
\li{\strong{The loader with the rule of section 6.1} (\code{\verb~|rlvm-load~} 58b0056c0417, published 01:2xZ on 2026-11-25; private distribution \code{\verb~|work/r2/dist-cand4~} = the jars above with this loader): suite \code{\verb~|rlvm-load~} 81 green (new: \code{\verb~|SplitTest.metadataAroundAnApplicationOfEagerReduceIsDeclinedUnderBothPolicies~}, ten variants); store digest IDENTICAL in all 14 reader configurations (the rule fires on none of those files) and the strict digests identical to the previous loader's; \code{\verb~|scripts/gate.sh --corpus all~}: PASS, 230 / 230, 0 declined, mutants 17,775 with exactly the counts above - in particular the metadata mutant corpus keeps agree 779 / declined 1,197: no agreement becomes a decline; the 1,239 review exports: one verdict changes, \code{\verb~|s3-mdata-eager-hidden-ok~} reject -> DECLINE (practical; strict: declined as before), so the practical mode has 6 opposite verdicts left, all "official reject, accepted" (kind T), and none of the kind "official accept, rejected"; Init, Std and reachability accepted through this loader (the digest shows the same store for all eight corpora).}
\li{\strong{The launcher with the safety net of section 6.1} (\code{\verb~|rlvm-main~} 3729609561e3, published 02:18Z on 2026-11-25 on top of PK1's 90f97a28c07a; written in a private copy, \code{\verb~|work/r2/main-copy~}, gated on the private distribution \code{\verb~|work/r2/dist-net~} = the published jars of 01:50Z (ref a20c24a26b7c, load 58b0056c0417, machine c2e04f2294ef; default engine: reference) with this jar, then applied to the tree): module suite 64 tests (61 run green, 3 opt-in; new \code{\verb~|SafetyNetTest~}, 9 tests, three fixtures of \code{\verb~|batch4~}); \code{\verb~|scripts/gate.sh --defaults --corpus all --hostile work/r2/exports/manifest.tsv~}: PASS - 230 / 230, 0 declined; mutants 17,775: SOUNDNESS 0, COMPLETENESS 0, agree 15,741, declined 2,034 (tutorial 11,780 / 480, bugs 2,590 / 102, prelude 839 / 8, mdata 532 / 1,444). Against the record above exactly 351 agreements became declines; file by file (one JVM per corpus, \code{\verb~|work/r2/net/all-*.tsv~}) all of them are correct rejects of mutants with a metadata record (67 + 37 + 247), no accepted file and no file without a metadata record changed. Self-test passed; the hostile rows of the R2 manifest (32, with the seven of \code{\verb~|batch4~}): agree 23, kind-T accepts 5, wrong accept 0, wrong reject 0, declined 4. \strong{The same gate through the executable} (\code{\verb~|--native~}, \code{\verb~|work/r2/dist-net-native~}: the published jars of 02:18Z, machine 123cba5f232e): PASS with the same counts. All 1,245 review exports (one JVM): four verdicts change, the four \code{\verb~|r2-mdata-beta-*-ok~} files reject -> DECLINE; no "official accept, rejected" row is left, the six opposite verdicts left are the kind T accepts; strict: 0 opposite (R2 19 official verdicts / 13 declined, S3 420 / 3, E1 92 / 0, S2 267 / 2, first review 418 / 1). Init, Std and reachability accepted as before (\code{\verb~|policy=practical~}, no second run).}
\li{\strong{Corpora}: section 7.}
\li{\p{\strong{Cost} (\src{bench/quiet.py} window, one worker, five alternating runs, CPU = user + sys, median \verb~|[~min, max\verb~|]~; "before" = the same distribution with the published reference jar ca1f9bd918bb):}
